Verse 1:
[Eb7]I will [Ab]follow Thee, my [Db]Savior, Wheresoe'er my lot may [Ab]be.
[Eb7]Where thou [Ab]goest I will [Db]follow; Yes, my [Ab]Lord, I'll [Eb7]follow [Ab]Thee.
[Ab]I will [Eb]follow Thee, my [Ab]Saviour, Thou didst [Db]shed Thy blood for [Eb]me;
[Eb7]And though [Ab]all men should forsake [Db]Thee; By Thy [Ab]grace I'll [Eb7]follow [Ab]Thee.

Refrain:
[Eb7]I [Ab]will follow [Db]Thee, [Ab]my Saviour,
[Eb7]Thou [Ab]didst [Db]shed [Ab]Thy [Eb7]blood [Ab]for me;
[Ab]And [Eb]though [Ab]all men [Db]should [Eb]forsake Thee;
[Eb7]By [Ab]Thy [Db]grace [Ab]I'll [Eb7]follow [Ab]Thee.

Verse 2:
[Eb7]Though [Ab]the road [Db]be rough [Ab]and thorny,
[Eb7][Ab]Trackless [Db]as [Ab]the [Eb7]foaming [Ab]sea,
[Ab]Thou [Eb]hast [Ab]trod this [Db]way [Eb]before me,
[Eb7][Ab]And [Db]I'll [Ab]gladly [Eb7]follow [Ab]Thee.

Verse 3:
[Eb7]Though [Ab]I [Db]meet [Ab]with tribulations,
[Eb7][Ab]Sorely [Db]tempted [Ab]though [Eb7]I [Ab]be;
[Ab]I [Eb]remember [Ab]Thou [Db]wast [Eb]tempted,
[Eb7][Ab]And [Db]rejoice [Ab]to [Eb7]follow [Ab]Thee.

Verse 4:
[Eb7]Though [Ab]Thou leadest [Db]me [Ab]through affliction,
[Eb7][Ab]Poor, [Db]forsaken [Ab]though [Eb7]I [Ab]be;
[Ab][Eb]Thou [Ab]wast [Db]destitute, [Eb]afflicted,
[Eb7][Ab]And [Db]I [Ab]only [Eb7]follow [Ab]Thee.

Verse 5:
[Eb7]Though [Ab]to [Db]Jordan's [Ab]rolling billows,
[Eb7]Cold [Ab]and [Db]deep, [Ab]Thou [Eb7]leadest [Ab]me,
[Ab]Thou [Eb]hast [Ab]crossed the [Db]waves [Eb]before me,
[Eb7]And [Ab]I [Db]still [Ab]will [Eb7]follow [Ab]Thee.
